WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.180
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.830
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.280
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.780
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.680
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.880
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.880
...all are your friends

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.790
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.390
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.590
I long to fly freely

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.790
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.690
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:12.190
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.780
Romeo had never imagined how arduous chimney sweeping would be.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.780
And what was worse,

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:40.980
Romeo returned exhausted from a day of work only to find himself denied a meal.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:45.180
But that evening a miracle was visited upon Romeo.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.580
It was a gift from an angel.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.980
Episode 9:

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.980
A Love Letter, By Moonlight

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.680
I'm positive -- there's got to be an angel up there.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.780
But how could I figure out a way to tell it "thank you"...?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.880
What's wrong?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.480
Hey!

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.480
Ohh! Lousy mongrel!!

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.580
Get over there!

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.580
You are NOT allowed into this room!

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:27.280
If you don't do as you're told, I'll have you made into a fur coat!

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:32.680
Why you STUPID cat!

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:37.680
Ah--! Mom!

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:39.580
What's going on??!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.980
What are you two staring at?!

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.280
Oh! I--uh--m...

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.880
Instead of the both of you sitting around here doing nothing,

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.580
...how's about getting off your butts and going to work?!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.780
You're going to make back that money you DRANK last night!

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.480
We've got 82 lira invested into this child!

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.180
You'll earn money today or get what's coming to you, got that?

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.380
All right, all right! I hear you!

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.480
Hey, you'd better get a move on before lightning strikes you twice!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.280
Yeah, yeah, I know!

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.280
Due to your slacking off...

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.180
Enough already!
Here we go!

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.580
Yes sir!

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.580
Step on it!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.780
Whoa......
Move it!

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.580
Huh?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.680
I'll leave you behind!

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.680
Boss! You forgot something!

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.880
Oh, whoops...

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.680
Hey, Romeo! How's it going?

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:28.480
So, I take it that this boy JUST arrived in Milan?

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:32.780
Well, yes, that's right...
but he's a tough little guy.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.980
No smoke gets through at all. I hope you can do something about it.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.580
It'll be fine -- really.
We're right on top of it.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:00.780
There's something stuck in there.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.380
It's a birds' nest!

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.080
It happens from time to time.

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:41.180
He finds a chimney, the bird.
Says, "Here's a nice warm place."

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.580
And so the bugger goes and plants his nest right into somebody's chimney.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.180
Some bird spent this summer with you -- right over your heads.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.280
Are you all right?

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:54.880
I'm fine.
I'll manage it.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.980
Say, thanks a lot...

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.380
...for putting out your best efforts for us.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:03.380
Thank you!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.380
Now, then, sir, that will be one lira, if you please.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.080
Oh! Yes, of course.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.280
Thank you kindly for your patronage, sir.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.580
Now, what would YOU like?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.580
Huh? Me?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.880
Yes. I hope I have something that you might...

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.580
Good gracious, no! Please pay no mind to the boy.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.880
Ah! That's it!

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.980
Here you are. It's a picture book.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.480
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:51.080
I... can't read.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.180
Heh. It's nothing to be ashamed of.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.580
Nowadays there are still more people who CAN'T read than who CAN.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.580
You should begin by learning little by little.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:04.180
Let's start with your name. Okay, now...

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.280
"What is your name?"

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.680
"What... is... your... name?"

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:14.580
Right!

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:16.680
That's how you read this.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.480
It's Romeo, right?

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:24.080
"My name is Romeo."

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.980
"My name is Romeo."

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.180
Right.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:30.880
"My name..."

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:32.280
"My name..."

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:33.480
"...is Romeo."

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.180
"...is Romeo."

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.880
My name is Professor Casela.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.580
Visit me again, and we can go over lesson two.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.180
Thank you...! Very much!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.680
I'll ask Alfredo to read it for me the next time we see each other.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.080
Piccolo!

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.280
Where WERE you?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.080
We found work at FOUR places today!

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.480
The last house was the worst...

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.380
...but they gave me some cheese, see?

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:25.380
I figured I could give it to you.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.980
What's that??

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:58.280
Another gift from the angel!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.180
What is it, I wonder?

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:13.580
A letter?

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.280
Gee, I wonder what it says.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.080
Hey, don't go pulling any pranks on me, Piccolo!

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:41.180
"What... is..."

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:46.380
They're the same!

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:50.580
This last line is the exact same sentence as that one!

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.080
"What is your name?"

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.480
Romeo wanted more than anything to meet the angel locked behind that door...

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:14.080
...to meet it, and express his profound gratitude.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.080
I don't like him.

00:11:56.580 --> 00:11:58.280
That Romeo kid.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.680
Romeo?

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:06.380
Then it dawned on me... I realized that he's ALWAYS staring at the door to that room!

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:09.780
He might've sniffed something out about our TREASURE in that room.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:14.780
We can't let down our guard...

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.780
If he even TRIES to get near that room...

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:21.780
I tell you he's going to smart for it!

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:26.280
Well... Y'know... he IS locked up...

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:30.080
NO! That kid's a slippery one!

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.280
We can't relax our attention for one second!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.680
"My name is Romeo."

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:49.480
It was the first sentence that Romeo had ever written.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.880
I'm going to give this to the angel.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.780
If I could just get that key...

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.080
All right...!

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:36.480
Keep it down!

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.880
What a racket!

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:55.980
All right, what gives?

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.880
Palmo! You did this, didn't you!

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.480
Is something up with Romeo?

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.980
Why, the door couldn't be... UNLOCKED, could it?

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.280
Palmo!

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:22.380
Palmo! Where are you?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.580
Anzelmo! You're still awake?

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.280
Sort off...

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.980
Palmo! Why are you here?

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:35.980
I wonder what's wrong...

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:38.980
Hmph! Good-for-nothing cat.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.580
I'll have Romeo clean this mess up tomorrow.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:43.380
So you can go ahead and get to bed.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:50.480
What's with you? Who gives a whoop about his guy...

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.780
Is there someone there?

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.280
I guess it was my imagination.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.780
SPATZA CAMINO!

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.580
Chimneys cleaned, right here!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:23.180
SPATZA CAMINO!

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:24.880
Spatza... camino...

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:25.780
Romeo!

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.880
What's wrong!? You won't get any customers by squeaking like a mouse!

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.780
Yes sir.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:35.680
What in blazes is wrong?! You've been on cloud nine all morning!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.480
I'm sorry.

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:40.380
For Pete's sake! Get it together, will you?

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.680
Hey, Rossi!

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.180
You pushin' the brush even in this weather?

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.880
Hey there! Hold up a second.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:50.280
Look at the weather! How's about a drink or two?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:54.980
Hey, I really would like to, but the wife, ya know, she...

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.980
I wonder what it says.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.980
It's Professor Casera!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:05.780
Yeah!

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:09.880
Hurry up, let's go.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:25.780
Why that...!

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.380
Well, if it isn't Romeo!

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:49.480
You seem to be in quite a hurry.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:52.780
Professor Casera!
I was looking for you!

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.480
For me? Did you need something?

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:59.080
Uh... Umm...

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.280
What is it, Romeo?

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:04.080
Don't hold back.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:05.480
Okay!

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.580
Ummm... I'd like you to read something for me.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.580
This is it.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:18.580
"I saw you in the garden today."

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:21.780
"And yesterday--and the day before--every day since your arrival."

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:26.080
"I wish from the bottom of my heart for a chance to speak with you."

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:28.480
"Please, tell me...
what is your name?"

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:33.580
Umm... and then... this one!

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:35.380
Let's see...

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:39.580
"Romeo, thank you very much for telling me your name."

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:44.180
"Tomorrow when everyone is sleeping, I will signal you with my music box."

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:46.680
"Please come extra-quietly and pay me a visit."

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.980
Eh?! Really?!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:51.880
Your girlfriend?

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.880
Hey! Romeo!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.480
What are you doing over here?!

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.280
Get over here right now!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.280
Prof. Casera, please keep this a secret!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.780
Please!

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.380
Yes, of course.

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.180
Thank you very much!

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:25.880
"Tomorrow when everyone is sleeping, I will signal you with my music box."

00:20:33.780 --> 00:20:34.980
It's the signal!

00:21:03.480 --> 00:21:04.580
Come in.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:59.080
Angeletta -- that's the angel's name.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.180
She says that because of her bad health,

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:04.880
...she's never ever been allowed to get a glimpse of the "real sky"!

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:08.080
I'll go and look for you!

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.880
Next time:
The Blue-Sky Sketchbook
See you then!

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:17.380
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:25.980 --> 00:22:30.080
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:34.380
seem to end so soon?

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:38.580
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:38.780 --> 00:22:42.780
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:43.390 --> 00:22:47.690
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:47.690 --> 00:22:51.590
Once again in the sky

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:58.890
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:04.490
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:08.690
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
